+# Bytes: an immutable run of bytes, each 0..255. In the theory it is a
+# list, as a U32 is a Word; compiled to C it is a slice (offset, length) of
+# one flat, reference-counted block, so a copy or a slice shares the block
+# and costs no byte. Data: stored, copied and sent freely.
+type Bytes is Data:
+  Bytes{data: List<&2, U32>}
+
